---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ExternalLink from '@/components/ExternalLink.astro';

// DRAFT: "Responding to a flood" guided path. Step text is VERBATIM from the
// coalition Workflows Running Notes (Response workflow, Day 1 to 2-3 weeks);
// links are wired as written in the source. Internal toolkit pages are plain
// links; external/Drive/YouTube resources use ExternalLink. The shared SignUp
// Genius LOGIN in the source is never rendered; the tool is named only.
const SHEET_DIRECTORY = 'https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1sJ-inMiVKj5SWsCukg_IimgWcA4oQLVWkbg6lAxcI3E/edit?gid=1691746306#gid=1691746306&range=A1';
const SIGNUP_GENIUS = 'https://www.signupgenius.com/';
const TRAINING = 'https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1wGL8dRUvuzBhJr3wQVdOE3eGHmT-lfxbpuH7wu-NqNQ/edit';
const TOOLKIT_OVERVIEW = 'https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1VoEHmsNMK4opUisOr4BHi6F6EJ4TmHUG';
const RESPONSE_KIT = 'https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ikZZYqIUHEduuEmD5WQdiV55Z2Jk-HAfGfPhBzUgUr0/edit';
const YT_BASEMENT_CLEANUP = 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S1OzbZ3Dn4M';
const YT_TRASH_PUMP = 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lyi1gdfURso';
const YT_SUMP_1 = 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ahviU2JVOTQ';
const YT_SUMP_2 = 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZVYbg8bxY1w';
const VOLUNTEER_MGMT_DRIVE = 'https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1QGrMJ_mv5LSGZ4ECDOuuOs9OJtcOfZY3';
const SHEET_TEMPLATES = 'https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1sJ-inMiVKj5SWsCukg_IimgWcA4oQLVWkbg6lAxcI3E/edit?gid=552434696#gid=552434696';
const EVENT_TEMPLATE = 'https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1sJ-inMiVKj5SWsCukg_IimgWcA4oQLVWkbg6lAxcI3E/edit?gid=825618087#gid=825618087&range=A14:D14';
const MOD_DIRECTORY = '/modules/emergency-preparedness/1-9';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Responding to a flood | Workflows | Resilience Hub Toolkit"
  description="The coalition's response workflow for flooding, from Day 1 to two to three weeks: standing up coordination, opening the hub, and running mucking days, each step linked to where it lives."
>
  <section class="py-12">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 max-w-3xl">
      <nav class="text-body-small text-muted-foreground mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/workflows" class="hover:text-primary underline underline-offset-2">Workflows</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true"> / </span>
        <span class="text-foreground">Responding to a flood</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="text-hero font-semibold mb-2 text-foreground">Responding to a flood</h1>
      <p class="text-label uppercase-accent text-primary mb-4">Response workflow for flooding, from Day 1 to 2-3 weeks</p>

      <!-- Safety lead note (Prem's guidance): volunteers stay out until the area is
           deemed safe; use the response phase to coordinate and build the plan. -->
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-card p-5 my-6 shadow-card">
        <p class="text-label uppercase-accent text-primary mb-1">Before sending volunteers out</p>
        <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground">
          Wait until your community has been deemed safe before sending volunteers
          out. Use this time to connect with your EMD, fire chief, and town
          managers, and to build a one-to-two-week sign-up volunteer plan to share
          via Front Porch Forum, social media, and other outlets.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Navigation video slot (coming later) -->
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-dashed border-primary/40 bg-muted p-5 my-8">
        <p class="text-label uppercase-accent text-primary mb-1">Walkthrough video, coming soon</p>
        <p class="text-body-small text-muted-foreground">
          A short video will walk through how to move through this response path. It
          is not recorded yet.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-title font-semibold text-foreground mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-border">In the event of a flood</h2>
      <ol class="space-y-4 list-decimal pl-5 text-body text-muted-foreground">
        <li>Contact local administrators/EMD/fire departments/community contacts on <a href={MOD_DIRECTORY} class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2">1.9: Directory of Local Leaders</a> <span class="text-body-small text-muted-foreground">(<ExternalLink href={SHEET_DIRECTORY}>open the live spreadsheet</ExternalLink>)</span> and/or regional leaders</li>
        <li>Identify areas of the community that were most severely impacted (surveying damage, asking fire chief/EMD, local facebook groups where people are posting photos of damage, get in car/on foot see the damage so when you start mucking and gutting you know where to send people)</li>
        <li>Contact other team members involved in response: <a href={MOD_DIRECTORY} class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2">1.9 Neighbor Directory</a>/<a href={MOD_DIRECTORY} class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2">1.9: Directory of Local Leaders</a></li>
        <li>Create spreadsheets using templates for this event, like <ExternalLink href={EVENT_TEMPLATE}>this one</ExternalLink></li>
        <li><a href="/modules/emergency-preparedness/1-10/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2">Coordinate Volunteers</a> to go door-to-door in communities to survey data using Crisis CleanUp and/or damage assessment forms. <a href="/modules/emergency-preparedness/1-10/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2">1.10 Volunteer Management</a></li>
        <li>
          Launch <ExternalLink href={SIGNUP_GENIUS}>sign-up genius</ExternalLink> for a few days or more, depending on severity
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mt-1">
            <li>Post link to sign up genius of FPF, social media, other outlets</li>
            <li>Automate the volunteer waiver in SignUp Genius</li>
            <li>Set up shifts to survey impacted areas, assess damage, and pump basements if needed</li>
            <li>If extensive mucking/gutting needs to be done, launch signup genius for two weeks (as far out as you can schedule)</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>Connect with <a href={MOD_DIRECTORY} class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2">1.9: Directory of Local Leaders</a> to access hub and tools/ response kit.</li>
        <li>When safe, set up and/or open hub for volunteers, response kit, take note of inventory, and gather needed tools <a href="/modules/emergency-preparedness/1-11/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2">1.11 Flood Recovery Supplies and Work</a></li>
        <li>
          Coordinate volunteers for mucking days. Identify team leads and volunteers with trucks to move pumps. <a href="/modules/emergency-preparedness/1-10/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2">1.10 Volunteer Management</a>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mt-1">
            <li>Create situation sheets</li>
            <li>Make sure volunteers have necessary tools, waivers and have had <ExternalLink href={TRAINING}>safety briefing/muck and gut training</ExternalLink></li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>Carpool when possible</li>
        <li>Clean tools upon return each day.</li>
        <li>Take inventory of what comes back/ file paperwork</li>
        <li>
          Continue to coordinate with Town Manager/ Fire Chief/ identified contacts
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mt-1">
            <li>Share reports as they request</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <!-- "How to use this kit": opens with a link to Prem's RAFT Response Kit doc
           (the pallet contents, shared anyone-with-link), then the grouped how-to
           resources from the source. -->
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-card p-5 my-6 shadow-card">
        <p class="text-label uppercase-accent text-muted-foreground mb-3">How to use this kit</p>
        <p class="text-body-small text-muted-foreground mb-3">See what goes in a response kit in the <ExternalLink href={RESPONSE_KIT}>RAFT Response Kit</ExternalLink> list, then use the guides below.</p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-body text-muted-foreground">
          <li>
            <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Basic overview</span>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mt-1">
              <li><ExternalLink href={TOOLKIT_OVERVIEW}>Toolkit overview of this work</ExternalLink></li>
              <li><ExternalLink href={YT_BASEMENT_CLEANUP}>How to Clean Up a Flooded Basement</ExternalLink></li>
              <li><ExternalLink href={TOOLKIT_OVERVIEW}>Field guide for cleanup of flooded homes</ExternalLink></li>
              <li><ExternalLink href={TOOLKIT_OVERVIEW}>Pumping out basements</ExternalLink></li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Trash water pump</span>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mt-1">
              <li><ExternalLink href={YT_TRASH_PUMP}>How to Use a Gas Trash Pump (Sunbelt Rentals Workshop Series)</ExternalLink></li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Sump pump</span>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mt-1">
              <li><ExternalLink href={YT_SUMP_1}>How to Pump Out a Flooded Basement #1, Water Removal, Water Pumping</ExternalLink></li>
              <li><ExternalLink href={YT_SUMP_2}>How to Pump Out a Flooded Basement #2, Water Removal, Water Pumping</ExternalLink></li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Mucking / gutting guide</span>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mt-1">
              <li><ExternalLink href={TOOLKIT_OVERVIEW}>Mucking and Gutting guide</ExternalLink></li>
            </ul>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-title font-semibold text-foreground mt-12 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-border">At the end of the response</h2>
      <ol class="space-y-3 list-decimal pl-5 text-body text-muted-foreground">
        <li>Clean everything</li>
        <li>Take inventory</li>
        <li>
          Send report out of what was completed to:
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mt-1">
            <li>State agencies</li>
            <li>Local agencies</li>
            <li>Long-term recovery groups</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="text-title font-semibold text-foreground mt-12 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-border">Resources for organizing an effective response</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-body text-muted-foreground mb-6">
        <li><ExternalLink href={TOOLKIT_OVERVIEW}>Community Resilience Toolkit</ExternalLink></li>
        <li><ExternalLink href={VOLUNTEER_MGMT_DRIVE}>Volunteer Management</ExternalLink></li>
        <li><ExternalLink href={SIGNUP_GENIUS}>SignUp Genius</ExternalLink></li>
      </ul>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-card p-5 shadow-card mb-6">
        <p class="text-label uppercase-accent text-muted-foreground mb-3">2-week response volunteer slots</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-body text-muted-foreground">
          <li><span class="text-foreground font-medium">Hub Coordinator:</span> at least 1 person all day there are volunteers</li>
          <li>
            <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Canvaser:</span> 1-2 for the first few days.
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mt-1">
              <li>Canvasing affected areas for needs</li>
              <li>Taking notes/ getting paperwork signed for job sites</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li><span class="text-foreground font-medium">Trash pump operator:</span> 1 per shift with truck is best.</li>
          <li><span class="text-foreground font-medium">Sump pump operator:</span> 1 per pump (two pumps per hub)</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-body-small text-muted-foreground mt-3 mb-1">Once homes are pumped:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-body text-muted-foreground">
          <li><span class="text-foreground font-medium">Mucking lead:</span> 1 Per team (two kits per hub)</li>
          <li><span class="text-foreground font-medium">Mucking volunteer:</span> 3-4 per team</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground mb-2">
        Create a spreadsheet to track work sites, volunteers, town/state contacts:
        <ExternalLink href={SHEET_TEMPLATES}>Spreadsheet templates</ExternalLink>
      </p>

      <nav class="flex items-center justify-between border-t border-border mt-10 pt-6 text-body-small" aria-label="Path navigation">
        <a href="/workflows/before" class="text-muted-foreground hover:text-primary underline underline-offset-2">&larr; Before a flood</a>
        <a href="/workflows/recover" class="text-primary font-medium underline underline-offset-2">Next: Recovering after &rarr;</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
